NAME
====

**jeep-list** - list system information

SYNOPSIS
========

**jeep-list** [**-J** | **--no-jpm**]

DESCRIPTION
===========

**jeep-list** lists system information, including the bundles installed in the
current __syspath__. By default, **jeep-list** will list both Janet bundles and
JPM bundles. The **--no-jpm** option can be used to exclude JPM bundles from the
results.

Options
-------

- **-J** | **--no-jpm**:
  Exclude JPM bundles from the listing.

For more information about __JPM bundles__, __Janet bundles__ and the
__syspath__, see CONCEPTS in `jeep(1)`.

EXAMPLES
========

To list system information, including all installed bundles:

````
$ jeep list
````

To list system information, showing installed Janet bundles only:

````
$ jeep list -J
````

